{"type": "fact", "id": "F132", "statement": "Morgan Hale died of burns in front of evac shelter B-19 on spring day 63 at about 7:47 AM, having survived 1 day 23 hours 47 minutes with no kills", "category": "self", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-12318", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F133", "statement": "Starting an in-progress clean water craft beside the burning pavement fire outside the shelter door set Morgan on fire; the fire burned legs, then the whole body, and ended the run within about 15 game seconds", "category": "hazard", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-11479", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F134", "statement": "When on fire, waiting in place or rolling on the ground tries to put the fire out but repeatedly failed to extinguish it; the burns cut strength and dexterity to 1, cause severe pain and break bones, and standing was a struggle", "category": "procedure", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-11742", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F135", "statement": "Interacting with shallow lake water offers consume it, pour into a container, or pour on the ground; filling plastic bottles from it gives two bottles of raw water", "category": "procedure", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-10373", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F136", "statement": "A lake trout is visible in the lake shallows just west of the field north of the shelter", "category": "resource", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-10321", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F137", "statement": "A batch of four clean water takes about 18 minutes 44 seconds (5 min 30 s for one), needs a nearby fire and 4 raw water on hand, and warns when there is no empty container to hold the result", "category": "procedure", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-11039", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F138", "statement": "Morgan wields the long pointy stick and carries a bow fire drill at 4/10, flashlight off, pocket knife, dead smartphone, 27+ cattail stalks, burdock, 2 crow eggs, a robin egg, a cardinal egg, 2 cooked cattail stalks and clean water; worn gear includes sling, messenger bag, jeans, emergency jacket, hand wraps, scarf and plastic shopping bag", "category": "item", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-9775", "stored": null}
{"type": "fact", "id": "F139", "statement": "Hand encumbrance from worn gear slows crafting to 90 percent", "category": "procedure", "observed": "bf01a9f1ca634ea63144b01cd8debe8d-9425", "stored": null}
